    "finalText": "The URL shortener is complete and fully verified. Final state:\n\n**Implementation**\n- `cmd/server/main.go` — reads `DATABASE_URL`, connects via pgx (database/sql driver), applies migrations, serves on `0.0.0.0:8000` in the foreground with graceful shutdown\n- `internal/store` — pgx-backed persistence: create (custom + generated 8-char codes), get, atomic click increment (`UPDATE ... RETURNING` guarantees exactly-once counting), and creation-ordered listing; SQL migrations embedded via `embed` + golang-migrate\n- `internal/api` — chi v5.2.1 router (version unchanged) with all five endpoints and JSON error bodies\n- `start.sh` — executable, runs the prebuilt binary (rebuilds only if missing); migrations apply before serving; no dependency installs\n- `README.md` — includes the required \"Starting the server\" section\n\n**Verification results** (all against live Postgres 16)\n- 201/409/404/422/302 status codes and JSON shapes match the spec exactly, including 4–20 char code edges and `{\"items\":[...],\"total\":n}` ordering\n- Restart test confirmed links and click counts survive (click 1 → 2 across a restart)\n- `sh start.sh` booted cleanly twice; database left empty for the test suite and port 8000 is free"
